+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+Requests a page of conversation summaries. The server accepts this frame regardless of the history opt-in; `limit`, when present, is an integer from 1 through 200, and `before`, when present, is a cursor with a parseable `updatedAt` and a `sessionId` ([validated by: accepts valid list requests and names invalid paging fields](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L23)).
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                                  |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                                       |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | Page size, an integer from 1 through 200                     |
+| `before` | object | No       | Cursor containing both `updatedAt` and `sessionId`           |
+
+The frame has no user id field. The server takes the user from the authenticated connection ([validated by: answers with the authenticated user's summaries, in wire-safe newest-first pages](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L48)).
+
+With history disabled, the server answers with an `error` frame whose code is `UNSUPPORTED` and sends no list ([validated by: refuses a list request with UNSUPPORTED when history is not enabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L116)).
+
 ## 5. Server-to-Client Messages
 
 ### 5.1 connected
